In this code snippet, you can write JavaScript to manipulate the browser or perform certain actions. For example, you can use JavaScript to update the page dynamically, handle user input, or make API requests. Remember to include appropriate comments and structure your code neatly for better readability.

```javascript
// Function to display a message when a button is clicked
function showMessage() {
  alert("Button clicked!");
}

// Event listener for the button click
document.getElementById('myButton').addEventListener('click', showMessage);
```

In this example, we define a function `showMessage` that displays an alert when the button with the ID 'myButton' is clicked. We then attach this function as an event listener to the button using `addEventListener`.

